WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
Welcome to the last chapter of
Building Ticket-to-Machine.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.862
Chapter 8: one writer per attribute.

3
00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:09.437
Two writers on one attribute
isn't drift you can fix.

4
00:00:09.437 --> 00:00:10.900
It's drift you've scheduled.

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.912
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
design makes Entra inbound provisioning

6
00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:20.625
the one writer into the directory, but
SailPoint can also provision Entra ID.

7
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:22.203
If both write department,

8
00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:26.187
the reconciliation reports drift
that the next sync recreates.

9
00:00:26.187 --> 00:00:30.094
This chapter compares the two
provisioning configurations,

10
00:00:30.094 --> 00:00:33.388
offline, and names every
attribute with two writers.

11
00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:35.810
Then two labs and the dangers.
